            "type": "text",
            "text": "Activate",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Cast a Spell"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "On certain rare occasions, when a particularly despoiled tree or a powerful demonic fungal infestation (such as a Jeharlu Spore) is destroyed, the grimy black ash that remains behind functions as a catalyst called black ash. A "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "9dfded9c-826b-57e9-989b-6b4ea568d4b8"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " empowered with this catalyst gains the fungus trait and appears diseased and toxic, with greasy filaments of dripping fungus growing through its vines. A creature damaged by this wall's thorns takes an additional "
          },
          {
            "type": "damage",
            "instances": [
              {
                "formula": "1d6",
                "damageType": "poison",
                "category": "persistent"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
